{"page_id": "olmo_table_tests-033c1efd2c0e15b829f9e9164f0e7bc1fecf_pg5_pg1-p1", "markdown": "objectives of the Master's degree in Management of Human resources, and a test, assigned upon application, aimed at evaluating the applicants' basic knowledge in the core areas of the MHR programme. Applicants might be interviewed for admission.\n\nMore details are available on the following MHR programme webpage: https://mhr.cdl. unimi.it/en/enrolment.\n\nLinks to enrolment information and procedures\n\nhttps://www.unimi.it/en/study/enrolment\n\nN° of places reserved to non-EU students resident abroad\n\n25\n\n1st COURSE YEAR Core/compulsory courses/activities\n\nLearning activity\n\nAdvanced Lahour Economics + Personnel Economics\n\nComparative and European Labour Law\n\nData Analysis and Statistics\n\nHR Infomation Systems.\n\nHuman Resources Management\n\nIntemational Business Management and Accounting\n\nOrganizational Behaviour\n\nEcts Sector\n\n12 SECS-P/01\n\n9 TUS/07\n\n6| SECS-S/03|\n\n9 SECS-P/10\n\n9 INF/01\n\n6 SECS-P/10\n\n9| M-PS1/06\n\nTotal number of compulsory credits/ects\n\n2nd COURSE YEAR Core/compulsory courses/activities\n\nLearning activity\n\nHiring and Recruitment\n\nEcts Sector\n\n6| SPS/09\n\nTotal number of compulsory credits/ects\n\nElective courses\n\nStudents must get 18 credits (CFU/ECTS) by choosing two courses from the following list.\n\nTo obtain the required 18 CTU/ECTS, students need to choose a maximum of one course in the M-PSI/06 or SPS/09 or\n\nSECS-P/01 areas.\n\nAdvanced Strategic Management\n\nComparative industrial relations\n\nCompensation and benefit\n\nConflict Management and Negotiation Empirical methods for inequality analysis Leaming and development\n\nOrganizational innovation and technology\n\nOrganizational Transformation and Change\n\n9(6) SECS SECS-P/D8, (3)\n\nSÉCS-P/07\n\n9 SPS109\n\n9 SECS-P/10\n\ng M-PS1/06\n\n9 SECS-P/01\n\n9 M-PS1/06ł\n\n9 (3) SECS-P/08, (6łą\n\nSECS-P/10\n\n9 SECS-P/10\n\nFurther elective courses\n\nStudents must get 9 CFU/ECTS by choosing one or more courses offered by the University of Milan. The course of choice has to award a final mark.\n\nPlease check https://mhr.cdl.unimi.it/en/courses/9-credit-courses.\n\nMoreover, students must get 3 CFU by choosing from internship, workshops, assessment of advanced computer skills, assessment of advanced knowledge foreign languages, traineeship abroad.\n\nPlease check https://mhr.cdl.unimi.it/en/courses/3-credit-activities.\n\nStudents who do not have an Italian qualification can choose to obtain 3 CFU in Additional language skills: Italian (for more details see the section Language test / computer literacy test)\n\nAdditional Language Skills: Italian (3 ECTS)\n\nAdvanced Language Skills: French (3 ECTS)\n\nAdvanced Language Skills: German (3 ECTS)\n\nAdvanced Language Skills: Spanish (3 ECTS)\n\n3/ ND\n\n3 ND\n\n3 ND\n\n3 ND\n\nEnd of course requirements\n\nTotal number of compulsory credits/ects\n\n15 NA\n\n15", "width": 1653, "height": 2339, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "objectives of the Master's degree in Management of Human resources, and a test, assigned upon application, aimed at evaluating the applicants' basic knowledge in the core areas of the MHR programme. Applicants might be interviewed for admission.", "bbox": {"x": 117.0265482922434, "y": 82.83958329173782, "width": 1399.4424778761063, "height": 92.5854166666666}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "More details are available on the following MHR programme webpage: https://mhr.cdl. unimi.it/en/enrolment.", "bbox": {"x": 117.02654842876115, "y": 185.17083332651137, "width": 1228.778761061947, "height": 34.110416666666545}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Links to enrolment information and procedures", "bbox": {"x": 87.76991123804494, "y": 238.77291665313072, "width": 575.3805309734514, "height": 29.237500000000157}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "https://www.unimi.it/en/study/enrolment", "bbox": {"x": 117.02654839057467, "y": 272.8833333157203, "width": 468.1